{
  "case_id": "2008-07-615",
  "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At the heart of this appeal is a matter of statutory construction. Respondent received $2.3 million in public funds under the Victims Protection and Terrorism Risk Insurance Act. TRIA provides, and this is at the blue brief, page 11a, that a party electing to receive such funds must relinquish rights with respect to enforcement against property that is at issue in claims against the United States before an international tribunal or that is the subject of awards by such tribunal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, they could have agreed that they have a bank account somewhere and any amounts would be set off by that. That wouldn't make that bank account at issue with respect to their claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you -- something that I would just like clarification on. You mentioned that the Cubic judgment is on appeal to the Ninth Circuit. It has been on appeal since June of '98?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What are the positions taken about that judgment by the respective sides, and why is it pending for ten years?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could -- let's assume that the -- that Iran is able to execute on the Cubic judgment. Could it take the proceeds out of the United States, given the 2007 blocking order?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But going back to the main issue, the only reason that this is at issue before the Iran tribunal is because it might be a setoff in the event of judgment in favor of Iran?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you -- can you articulate a general test in a sentence or two about how you decide whether particular assets are at issue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But that's not saying that. Isn't that -- that issue is moot?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But how is that affected -- how is that affected depending on whether or not the judgment is executed or not. Would the Iran tribunal have the authority to order Cubic not to satisfy the judgment, but to just hold the funds?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Right. So what is the -- it seems at the moment, frankly you could read it either way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That creates the issue, because the question is whether money that never goes back to Iran, but rather goes to an attaching person, is money that is or money that is not subtracted from the amount that the United States owes Iran."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why not? I mean, the question I raised before, why wouldn't the United States be urging that it gets credit, whether Iran gets the money or whether the people who are creditors of Iran get the money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bederman",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The panel makes very clear that under the sales contract credit has to be given to Iran for its advance payment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "question to Respondent's counsel, the one thing I would point out to you again, is another clue in the statute.\nIf we look at the Victims Protection Act, which was the predecessor statute here, section 2002(c), what Congress wanted to protect is the right of the United States to, quote, pursue these subrogated rights as claims or offsets of the United States in appropriate ways."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We would support, obviously, reversal of the lower court's opinion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-615",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc9393b53c6101b68af1dc76c39b4047267c45795539479d8e5c45a9988f7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc9393b53c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel.\nThe case is submitted."
    },
    {
